BEGIN:VEVENT
CREATED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260508T001525Z
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T193000
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260526T180000
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260508T001525Z
LAST-MODIFIED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260508T001525Z
UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482573
DESCRIPTION:Please register on either Meetup (https://www.meetup.com/pnw-
 software-quality-professionals-pnsqc/events/314648123/) or Luma (https:/
 /luma.com/60m4kgqw) so we can count attendance!&#13\;\n&#13\;\nConverge 
 with your fellow software professionals this May at Steeplejack on NE Br
 oadway!&#13\;\n&#13\;\nWhat are project managers actually saying about A
 I\, quality\, and delivery — and what does it mean for us in QA? Jahzeel
  Ormeño\, Founder and Principal Consultant of SimplexityPM\, is bringing
  the conversation from the PMI Portland Annual Conference straight to ou
 r Meetup with her informal talk &quot\;From the PMI Conference Floor: Wh
 at the PM World Is Saying About Quality\, AI\, and Getting Work Done Rig
 ht&quot\;.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nJahzeel is excited to debrief her experience f
 rom the conference with an honest conversation about what PMs are actual
 ly talking about: where AI is showing up (and where it isn’t)\, what els
 e dominated the room\, and how the PM practices most of us take for gran
 ted connect directly to software quality outcomes. Come ready to share w
 hat you’re seeing on your end too — the best part will be comparing note
 s.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nYou don’t need to be a PM to get something out of this
 . It’s a good fit if you’re curious about any of the following:&#13\;\n•
  What PMs and quality folks have in common (and where they still talk pa
 st each other)&#13\;\n• How AI is actually landing in delivery teams — b
 eyond the hype&#13\;\n• Which PM habits quietly prevent quality problems
  before they start&#13\;\n• Continuing the conversations from PMI Portla
 nd 2026&#13\;\n&#13\;\nThis will be a hybrid meetup\, so mingle in perso
 n or tune in online. Doors (and virtual lobby) open at 6pm for a half ho
 ur of pre-talk networking.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nSchedule:&#13\;\n&#13\;\n6pm -
  6:30pm Networking (online included)&#13\;\n6:30pm - 7:30pm ‎Open discus
 sion led by Jahzeel&#13\;\n&#13\;\n(While free to attend\, food and drin
 ks from the delicious Steeplejack menu will not be covered.)\n\nTags: pm
 \, pmi\, project management\, agile\, AI\, automation\, engineer\, leade
 rship\, networking\, process\, qa\, quality assurance\, software\, softw
 are quality\, software testing\, tech\, technologies\, technology\, test
 \, testing\, tooling\n\nImported from: http://calagator.org/events/12504
 82573
URL:https://luma.com/60m4kgqw
SUMMARY:PNSQC May Meetup: From the PMI Floor - an honest conversation on 
 AI
LOCATION:Steeplejack Brewing Company: 2400 NE Broadway\, Portland\, OR 97
 232\, Portland OR 97232 United States
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
CREATED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T160753Z
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260527T193000
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260527T180000
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T160753Z
LAST-MODIFIED;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260502T160753Z
UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482556
DESCRIPTION:#### Topic&#13\;\n&#13\;\nWriting proper alt text is hard. Bu
 t it doesn't have to be. There's a minimum standard and an advanced appr
 oach. People who need alt text will appreciate you for the former and lo
 ve you for the latter. Alt text is also a whole lot more than the `alt` 
 attribute. That's just one of the many ways to make content accessible. 
 In fact\, there are a number of considerations for writing great alt tex
 t.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nIn this presentation\, Mark Wyner will help you unders
 tand the spectrum of options so you can take good care of your audience.
  We'll walk through implementation methods\, phonetics\, composition\, c
 omplex sources\, and tackling social media.&#13\;\n&#13\;\nLet’s give sc
 reen readers and other assistive technologies something to *talk* about.
 &#13\;\n&#13\;\n#### Agenda&#13\;\n&#13\;\nThe event begins at 6 pm\; jo
 in early\, starting at 5:45 pm for networking.&#13\;\n&#13\;\n* 5:45 Net
 working&#13\;\n* 6:00 Introductions and announcements&#13\;\n* 6:15 Pres
 entation&#13\;\n* 6:45 Q&amp\;A and discussion&#13\;\n&#13\;\n#### About
  the presenter&#13\;\n&#13\;\n[Mark Wyner](https://markwyner.com/) is an
  autodidactic polymath with over two decades of experience in design and
  development. His approach prioritizes usability\, accessibility\, and i
 nclusivity. He’s also an antifascist humanitarian. So diversity and equi
 ty are overarching principles for everything he does in this space. Curr
 ently\, as the Lead Product Designer at BookNook. His pronouns are he/hi
 m/his. You can follow him on Mastodon or his accessibility writings on h
 is website.&#13\;\n&#13\;\n#### Accommodation requests&#13\;\n&#13\;\nIf
  you have any accommodation requests\, don't hesitate to contact us befo
 re the event to discuss.\n\nTags: User Research\, a11y\, accessibility\,
  accessibility lawsuits\, accessible technology\, accessible web design\
 , disability\, human rights\, inclusive design\, meetup:event=314591176\
 , meetup:group=Portland-Accessibility-and-User-Experience-Meetup\, mobil
 e user experience\, screen reader\, structured negotiation\, technology\
 , universal design\, usability\, user experience\, wcag\, web accessibil
 ity\, web design\n\nImported from: http://calagator.org/events/125048255
 6
URL:https://pdxa11yux.org/events/2026/05/27/alt-text-is-the-ocean-you-tho
 ught-was-a-pond.html
SUMMARY:Portland Accessibility and User Experience Meetup (PDX A11Y UX) -
  Alt Text is the Ocean You Thought Was a Pond
LOCATION:Albina Library\, Community Room 1A: 205 NE Russell St\, Portland
  OR 97212 US
SEQUENCE:2
END:VEVENT
